# sdlc-automation-agent Welcome Guide

## When to Fire

This rule fires when ALL of these are true: 
1. The sdlc-automation-agent plugin is loaded (this rule exists)
2. No `.sdlc-automation-agent/` directory exists in the project root
3. The user's first message is a development-related request (build, add, review, test, etc.)
4. The user has NOT been shown this welcome message already this session

**Do NOT fire** if:
- `.sdlc-automation-agent/` already exists (the session-start hook handles returning users)
- The user explicitly asks for something unrelated to development
- The user is already in a `/sdlc-automation-agent` session

## Action

Before responding to the user's request, briefly present the sdlc-automation-agent quick-start:

```python
AskUserQuestion(questions=[{
  "question": "This project has the sdlc-automation-agent pipeline plugin active.\n\n" 
    "**Just describe what you want** — the orchestrator auto-routes to the right agents.\n\n"
    "**For existing codebases:** run `/sdlc-automation-agent` first to map dependencies and architecture.\n\n"
    "How would you like to proceed?", 
  "header": "sdlc-automation-agent Pipeline Available", 
  "options": [
    {"label": "Start building (Recommended)", "description": "Describe what you want — init, config, and routing handled automatically"},
    {"label": "Reverse-engineer first", "description": "Run /sdlc-automation-agent to understand existing codebase before building"},
    {"label": "Work without the pipeline", "description": "Use Claude Code normally — invoke /sdlc-automation-agent anytime later"},  
    {"label": "Tell me more", "description": "Explain the 9 agents, delivery lifecycle, and how it works"}
  ],
  "multiSelect": false
}]) 
```

## Response Handling

- **"Start building"**: Invoke `Skill(skill="sdlc-automation-agent")` with the user's original request. The orchestrator auto-detects missing config and initializes if needed.
- **"Reverse-engineer first"**: Invoke `Skill(skill="sdlc-automation-agent")` with prompt "understand this codebase". After it completes, ask the user what they want to build.
- **"Work without the pipeline"**: Proceed normally with the user's request. No further pipeline reminders this session. Respect the choice fully.
- **"Tell me more"**: Provide a concise overview:

### Overview Response (for "Tell me more")

```
sdlc-automation-agent turns Claude Code into a multi-agent delivery system:

AGENTS (9)
  Product Manager       — Requirements, user stories, BRD
  Solution Architect    — System design, ADRs, API contracts
  Software Engineer     — Backend, frontend, AI/ML, mobile modes
  Quality Engineer      — Tests (unit, integration, e2e, performance)
  Compliance Engineer   — OWASP, STRIDE, HIPAA, pentest mode
  Code Reviewer         — Code quality, architecture conformance
  Platform Engineer     — Docker, CI/CD, Terraform, SLOs, runbooks 
  Technical Writer      — API docs, dev guides, sprint reports
  Research Advisor      — Thinking partner, ideation

DELIVERY LIFECYCLE
  Scrum:  Inception → Sprint Planning → Execution → Review → Close → loop
  Kanban: Discover → Ready → Execute → Review → loop  
  Per-story pipeline: SE → QE → CR → DoD evaluation

MODES — the orchestrator auto-routes:
  sprint · kanban · debug · explore · preview · status
  branch-finish · discover · story-buddy · retro · report
  release · reverse · stabilize · modernize · init · update 

COMMAND 
  /sdlc-automation-agent      — everything (or just describe what you need)
``` 

Then re-present the options.
